  "notes": "Cash basis. Governmental data from Statement of Receipts, Disbursements and Changes in Fund Balances (p4, Total column; General + Debt Service). Beginning cash = beginning fund balance as restated 1,171,359 (previously reported 1,534,707, restatement -363,348). Water and Sewer enterprise fund (p5-6) is business-type: beginning net position as restated 985,008; check 985,008 + 866,892 - 1,025,606 - 158,530 = 667,764. Business-type receipts/disbursements totals are summed (statement prints operating and nonoperating pieces separately; 'Principal and interest on loans' (47,803) is a negative nonoperating item treated as a disbursement); they match the Statement of Activities (p2) 830,217 / 1,025,606. Balance sheet uses the cash-basis Statement of Net Position Total column (p1; governmental + business-type); governmental-only fund balances on p3. Detail: only the All Funds budgetary schedule (p7) exists; its mixed lines were split between governmental and business-type using pp4, 6 (budget_final only printed on combined lines, so null on split lines). The all-funds schedule printed totals (3,764,063 / 3,790,353) are the sum of both fund types. Transfers in 158,530 (General fund) and out 158,530 (Water/Sewer) from p4/p6/p7. Read pages 1-7 of 7"
